The main changes: the subfield count is computed once instead of on every iteration, and `operator==` replaces `compare() == 0`. `operator==` checks lengths before comparing characters, so mismatched names are rejected faster. Results are identical, including the return value when no match is found.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 FieldBase::GetSubField(const std::string& subFieldName) const
{
    const FIT_UINT16 numSubFields = this->GetNumSubFields();
    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < numSubFields; i++) {
        if (this->GetSubField(i)->name == subFieldName)
            return i;
    }

    return FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD;
}
```